ies.jpg","caption":"FLASHBACK TO 1934, shows Belgrave's cross-country runners and officials with their trophy collection which includes the London-Brighton (News of the World) Trophy, Southern and Surrey County cups. The team was also placed in the National and South of Thames Senior and Junior races.\nBACK ROW (l.to r.):E.A.Duffett,R.Savage,A.T.Jordan,B.Lindsey,S.T.Ring,F.R.Webb,N.Dewberry, A. Robertshaw, W. Mitchell, A. Patience, L. Rollins.\nCENTRE ROW (l. to r.):T.Eaton(masseur),D.Patience,R.Patience,J.Belchamber(Past President), W.H.Hare(Hon.Tresurer),J.R.McKay(President),W.Bayliss(General Hon.Secretary),E.Gordon(Past President),F.Walker,C.Penny,WG.Webb.\nFRONT ROW (l. to r.):W.Rice,C.T.Carter,H.W.Shields,J.Flower,A.W.Penny,S.Warboys,A.Shaw, A.Taylor,[illegible].E.Footer(Captain), A.Allum.","source":"B172-66","when":"December 1969"},"x":1,"share":{"d":"W. H. Hare in The Belgravian, the Belgrave Harriers club gazette, 1925–1976: 23 mentions in 20 issues, 13 race results and 2 photographs. Wrote or reported 5 items.","img":"https://belgravian-images.stephendgardner.workers.dev/belgravian/crops/B20/B20-p3-w-h-hare.jpg","u":"https://stephengardner1.github.io/belgrave-harriers-data/belgravian/read/share/p-w-h-hare.html"},"legend":false}